Included third-party material
================================================================================

Shopping Queries Dataset (ESCI)
  Copyright Amazon.com, Inc. or its affiliates. All Rights Reserved.
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt).
  Source: https://github.com/amazon-science/esci-data
  Paper:  Reddy et al., "Shopping Queries Dataset: A Large-Scale ESCI
          Benchmark for Improving Product Search", 2022.
          https://arxiv.org/abs/2206.06588

  Files in this repository that contain material from ESCI, and how it was
  changed:

  sample/queries.csv, sample/docs.parquet, sample/labels.csv
      8 queries, the 176 products a person graded for them, and those
      grades. Product descriptions and bullet points are joined into one
      `body` field and cut to 300 characters. ESCI's E/S/C/I labels are
      converted to grades 3/2/1/0.

  experiments/judge-negation-audit/results/negation_pairs.csv
  experiments/judge-negation-audit/results/negation_answers.csv
      Query text, product titles, and description excerpts for the pairs
      in the negation audit, and short quotes from them in the rater's
      answers.

  experiments/*/results/*.csv
      ESCI query and product identifiers, alongside grades and rankings
      produced by this project's runs. The judge-truncation results also
      include ESCI's human labels as grades 3/2/1/0.

  The ESCI dataset itself is downloaded by scripts/01_download_esci.sh and
  is not included.


